items.description:
In execute(), query result cell values (row[i] and headers from azColName[i]) are concatenated directly into a Markdown table without escaping the pipe character or other Markdown-significant characters:

  ss << row[i] << (i+1 == row.size() ? " |\n" : " | ");

If a stored value (or column name) contains '|', it will break the table structure; if it contains crafted content (e.g. newlines, markdown images/links, or instruction-looking text), the tool output returned to the LLM is effectively a reflection of attacker-influenced DB content into the agent context. This is a weak prompt-injection / markdown-injection surface whenever DB content is untrusted (e.g. user-supplied data, web-fetched insertions). Values should be escaped (e.g. replace `|` with `\|`, sanitize newlines) to keep the table well-formed and avoid injecting spurious Markdown/instruction text into the model context.

